## Facts (from `doc/plan/c016-worklog/bucketB-java-samples-summary.md`)
- Native REQUEST probe: every functional request returned `SubmitResult.OK` — not a D-B85 or handover
  issue. Cause is sample sequencing: `DispatchWorker.dispatch()` calls `offers.offer(...)` (which
  records `deadline = now + 900 ms`, `DeliveryOfferStore.java:21-30`, `SampleTimings.java:11`) BEFORE
  awaiting `publishStatus(...)` and submitting the courier actor send (`DispatchWorker.java:36-40`,
  re-dispatch `:80-83`). In the failing run the preceding `DeliveryStatusChangedReq` took 2.653 s, so
  attempt 1 expired before courier A even received `OfferDeliveryMsg`; the courier's valid decision was
  then dropped as stale, attempt 2 expired the same way, and the client stream sequence timed out
  (`gate-samples-java-DeliveryDispatch.log:234-247`).
- Sample contract `framework/doc/framework/common/sample/deliverydispatch/README.ko.md:292-296` (§7.2):
  the attempt expires when courier A does not answer within the deadline **after receiving** the offer.
  The other languages' DeliveryDispatch implementations (cpp/dotnet/node) can be read for parity on
  where the offer row/deadline starts — read only.
- Env: `TMPDIR=/dev/shm/zlink-tmp-java`, `flock -w7200 /tmp/zlink-jvm-gate.lock`,
  `ZLINK_LIBRARY_PATH=/home/hep7/project/zlink/.artifacts/wsl/install/zlink-core/0.17.0/lib/libzlink.so`
  (a file), Docker OK. Run: `cd framework/languages/java/samples/java/DeliveryDispatch && ./run_sample.sh`.
  Known unrelated: `courier-session` `TEARDOWN_FAILED` at shutdown (pre-existing C) may still make the
